        "approval_content": "# Fast execute script - BlueKing - 37 execute object(s)\n\n## Operation summary\n\n| Item | Content |\n| --- | --- |\n| Operation type | Fast execute script |\n| Resource scope | BlueKing(biz:2) |\n| Initiator | admin |\n| **Risk level** | **High** |\n| Operation object | Clean disk cache |\n| Total execute objects | 37 |\n| **High-risk statement detection** | **High-risk statement rule matched, please check carefully** |\n| **Dynamic target notice** | **Target contains dynamic group or topo node, the actual machines are resolved again on release and may differ from here** |\n| [Default] Timeout | 7200 |\n\n## Script content\n\n`script_content`\n\n```\n#!/bin/bash\nrm -rf /tmp/cache\n```\n\n## Raw parameters\n\n```json\n{\n  \"script_content\" : \"See the [Script content] section\",\n  \"script_param\" : \"******\"\n}\n```\n"
    }
}
```

### Response Parameters

{% include '_generic_v4_response.md.j2' %}

#### data

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| approval_task_id | string | Approval task ID |
| expire_at | long | Expiry moment of the approval task, Unix timestamp in milliseconds. After expiry the task can no longer be released |
| approval_content | string | Approval content in Markdown, already rendered by the Job platform, which the channel can present directly. It contains, in order, a level-one title (such as "Fast execute script - BlueKing - 37 execute object(s)"), the summary table (operation type, resource scope, initiator, risk level, operation object, total execute objects, defaults that took effect, and so on), the script content code block and the raw parameters JSON code block. Per-step details (step name, execute account, script name, target host list, and so on) are not expanded in the body, so that an over-long ticket does not push the approver to scroll straight to the bottom and release it, but they still feed into the risk level. High-risk items that must stand out (matched high-risk statement rules, dynamic group targets) are rendered in Markdown bold. The values of password-like sensitive fields are placeholders only and carry no real value, **script content being the single exception shown as is**. When the target contains dynamic groups or topology nodes, the body states that the machines actually executed on are resolved again at release time |
